review_comments.body:
**Suggestion: test deep-copy of `Artifact` and `Template` pointers too**

The test verifies `RedoScope` slice independence but doesn't verify that `Artifact` and `Template` pointer fields are independent copies. While both `RootfsArtifactInfo` and `Res`/`Ret` currently contain only value-type fields, adding a pointer/slice/map to either type in the future would silently create a shared reference.

Consider adding assertions like:

```go
// Verify Artifact pointer independence
src.Artifact = &sandboxtypes.RootfsArtifactInfo{Status: "old"}
dst := cloneTemplateImageJobInfo(src)
dst.Artifact.Status = "changed"
if src.Artifact.Status == "changed" {
    t.Fatal("Artifact should be deep-copied")
}

// Verify Template pointer independence
src.Template = &sandboxtypes.TemplateInfo{Ret: &sandboxtypes.RetInfo{RetMsg: "old"}}
dst = cloneTemplateImageJobInfo(src)
dst.Template.Ret.RetMsg = "changed"
if src.Template.Ret.RetMsg == "changed" {
    t.Fatal("Template.Ret should be deep-copied")
}
```

This would make the guard-rails described in the doc comment testable.

