review_comments.body:
**The retry failure returns success silently.** When both the initial `runTemplateJobCleanup` and the retry fail, the function logs a second WARN and returns `nil` (success). The orphaned job rows are unreconciled — there is no periodic cleanup or reconciliation loop to retry later.

Since the metadata is already deleted, the snapshot IS effectively gone, so returning success is correct. But the retry failure should be logged at ERROR level (not WARN) so it's visible in production incident triage — orphan job rows will cause the same `ListTemplates` bug if a new snapshot is created with the same ID.

```suggestion
	if err := runTemplateJobCleanup(ctx, snapshotID); err != nil {
		log.G(ctx).Warnf("snapshot %s job cleanup failed after metadata delete: %v", snapshotID, err)
		if retryErr := runTemplateJobCleanup(ctx, snapshotID); retryErr != nil {
			log.G(ctx).Errorf("snapshot %s job cleanup retry failed: %v, orphan job rows may remain", snapshotID, retryErr)
		}
		success = true
		return nil
	}
```

