review_comments.body:
Using `t.Fatal` inside a gomonkey-patched function is fragile — it calls `runtime.Goexit()` on the goroutine the patch runs on. If the function is ever called on a different goroutine in a future refactor, cleanup behavior becomes unpredictable. Prefer a spy counter pattern:

```go
getJobInfoCallCount := 0
patches.ApplyFunc(GetTemplateImageJobInfo, func(...) {
    getJobInfoCallCount++
    return nil, nil
})
// ... after executeSnapshotDeleteJob ...
if getJobInfoCallCount != 0 {
    t.Fatalf("GetTemplateImageJobInfo called %d time(s)", getJobInfoCallCount)
}
```

