review_comments.body:
**Brittle `else` fallthrough assumes ExportModeDocker.** This function is only called when `ExportMode == ExportModeDocker || ExportMode == ExportModeNative` (ext4.go:132), but the bare `else` at line 100 silently assumes the only other option is Docker. If someone later adds `ExportModeDockerless` to the caller's filter, this would attempt `docker create` on a dockerless source — producing a confusing error or, worse, pulling via docker against a ref never validated for that path.

An explicit guard would prevent future misuse:
```go
} else if source.ExportMode == ExportModeDocker {
    // ... existing docker path ...
} else {
    return fmt.Errorf("export mode %q not supported for streaming ext4 build", source.ExportMode)
}
```

